# Line endings are normalised for source files so diffs and merges behave; the persistent
# document fixtures are the exception.
#
# `tests/golden/*.p1doc` is byte-compared against what the serializer emits -- that is the
# strongest statement the golden test makes, and it is the property that catches a field being
# added to the canonicaliser without being added to the parser. On Windows, `core.autocrlf`
# rewrote those files' line endings to CRLF on checkout, which broke all three byte-identity
# assertions with a diff consisting entirely of `\n` versus `\r\n`.
#
# `-text` tells git not to apply any eol conversion to these paths: they are compared as
# bytes, so the bytes are the file.
tests/golden/*.p1doc -text

# The generated asset payloads are a build input, not source.
tests/golden/generated-assets.txt -text
